// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`build_drawing_set > lays out the Figures, writes the sheets, the PDF and the receipt, and updates the Filing Manifest 1`] = `
{
  "drawings": [
    "FIG-1.scene.json",
    "FIG-1.svg",
    "FIG-2.scene.json",
    "FIG-2.svg",
    "drawings-compliance.md",
    "drawings.pdf",
    "review",
    "rounds.json",
    "sheet-1.svg",
  ],
  "manifestSheets": [
    "| Drawing sheets | 1 (measured: the sheet-N.svg files in drawings/) |",
    "| Drawings | drawings/ (Drawing Sheets) | 1 |",
  ],
  "pdfHeader": "%PDF-1.4",
  "receipt": "# Drawing Set check receipt

- Office: US
- Page size: A4
- Drawing Sheets: 1
- Date: <date>
- Results: 23 pass, 0 fail, 1 not checked

This file lists each code check, the rule it applies and its result. It is not a verdict on the drawings. The rules a person must judge (sufficient views, every claimed feature shown, suitable legends) are not checked here; the attorney reviews them.

## Checks

| Check | Rule | Result | Detail |
|---|---|---|---|
| page-size | 37 CFR 1.84(f); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 2(2); PCT Rule 11.5 (A4 for all, Letter for the USPTO only; one size per application) | pass | 1 sheet(s), all A4 210 x 297 mm, short side at the top. |
| margins | 37 CFR 1.84(g), (t); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(1), Art. 2(5); PCT Rule 11.6(c), 11.7 (top 25, left 25, right 15, bottom 10 mm; nothing in the margin) | pass | Every Figure, label and sheet number is inside the 170.00 x 262.00 mm sight. |
| no-frame | 37 CFR 1.84(g); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(1); PCT Rule 11.6(c) (no frame around the sight) | pass | No frame and no drawn element outside the Figures. |
| glyph-height | 37 CFR 1.84(p)(3); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(2)(g); PCT Rule 11.13(h) (0.32 cm minimum at sheet scale) | pass | Smallest glyph at sheet scale: 3.22 mm (minimum 3.2 mm). |
| label-larger-than-numerals | 37 CFR 1.84(t), (u)(2); GL A-IX 4.2, 5.2 (FIG labels and sheet numbers larger than the reference signs) | pass | Labels and sheet numbers at least 6.00 mm; numerals up to 4.50 mm. |
| single-figure-no-label | 37 CFR 1.84(u)(1); GL A-IX 5.2; PCT IP 5.141 (a single Figure is not numbered and carries no "FIG.") | not-checked | 2 Figures; the rule applies to one. |
| figure-labels | 37 CFR 1.84(u)(1); GL A-IX 5.2; PCT Rule 11.13(k), IP 5.141 ("FIG." / "Fig.", consecutive Arabic numerals, partial views as number plus capital letter) | pass | FIG. 1, FIG. 2. |
| sheet-numbering | 37 CFR 1.84(t); PCT AI Section 207(b)(iii), Rule 11.7 ("n/N"); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 2(5), GL A-IX 4.2 (consecutive integer); centred at the top of the sight | pass | "n/N" 1 to 1, centred at the top of the sight. |
| orientation | 37 CFR 1.84(i) (top of a sideways sheet on the right); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(2)(h); PCT Rule 11.13(j) (top of the Figures on the left) | pass | 1 upright sheet(s), 0 sideways with the Figure top on the right. |
| text-keywords | 37 CFR 1.84(o); MPEP 507(C); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(2)(j); PCT Rule 11.11 (a few short keywords; flowcharts and block diagrams excepted) | pass | No Figure has more than 3 words of legend text (flowcharts and block diagrams excepted). |
| no-scale-text | 37 CFR 1.84(k); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(2)(c); PCT Rule 11.13(d) (no "actual size" or "scale 1:2") | pass | No scale or "actual size" text. |
| pdf-format | USPTO Patent Center PDF Guidelines; PCT Annex F 3.1.2 (PDF 1.4 to 1.6, fonts embedded, unencrypted, one page per sheet, A4 or Letter) | pass | PDF 1.4, 1 page(s), fonts embedded, not encrypted. |
| part-without-numeral | CONTEXT.md Figure ("every part drawn has one"); 37 CFR 1.84(p)(5); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(2)(i) | pass | No finding. |
| numeral-without-port | 37 CFR 1.84(q) ("extend to the feature indicated"); GL A-IX 7.5.1 | pass | No finding. |
| numeral-not-allowed | 37 CFR 1.84(p)(5); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(2)(i); PCT Rule 11.13(l) | pass | No finding. |
| numeral-two-parts | 37 CFR 1.84(p)(4); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(2)(i); PCT Rule 11.13(m) | pass | No finding. |
| lead-lines-cross | 37 CFR 1.84(q) ("Lead lines must not cross each other") | pass | No finding. |
| lead-line-off-part | 37 CFR 1.84(q) ("extend to the feature indicated"); GL A-IX 7.5.1 | pass | No finding. |
| lead-line-far-from-numeral | 37 CFR 1.84(q) ("originate in the immediate proximity of the reference character") | pass | No finding. |
| lead-line-missing | 37 CFR 1.84(q) (lead line required unless the numeral is underlined); PCT IP 5.145 | pass | No finding. |
| glyph-too-small | 37 CFR 1.84(p)(3); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(2)(g); PCT Rule 11.13(h) (0.32 cm minimum) | pass | No finding. |
| text-beyond-keywords | 37 CFR 1.84(o); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(2)(j) ("a few short keywords"); PCT Rule 11.11; 37 CFR 1.84(k) (no scale text) | pass | No finding. |
| numeral-overlap | 37 CFR 1.84(p)(3) ("should not cross or mingle with the lines") | pass | No finding. |
| numeral-on-line | 37 CFR 1.84(p)(3) ("should not cross or mingle with the lines", not on hatched surfaces); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(2)(b) | pass | No finding. |

## Review rounds

| Figure | Rounds the model saw | Latest render |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | 1 | review/FIG-1.round-1.png |
| 2 | no render seen | - |
",
  "result": "Built the Drawing Set of 2 Figure(s) on 1 A4 sheet(s) for US: drafting/hinge/drawings/sheet-1.svg, drafting/hinge/drawings/drawings.pdf, and the receipt drafting/hinge/drawings/drawings-compliance.md. Review renders of the sheets are in drafting/hinge/drawings/review/.
Receipt: 23 pass, 0 fail, 1 not checked.
No code check fails.
Updated drafting/hinge/filing-manifest.md: 1 drawing sheet(s), measured.
Report the receipt by check. The rules a person must judge (sufficient views, every claimed feature shown) stay with the attorney; never call the drawings compliant or ready to file.",
  "review": [
    "FIG-1.round-1.png",
    "FIG-2.round-1.png",
    "sheet-1.png",
  ],
}
`;

exports[`build_drawing_set > refuses with no Figure, on a proposed part, on a figure-list Error and on a coverage gap 1`] = `
{
  "coverageGap": "The Drawing Set was not built. 1 Error(s) of the figure list are open; fix each in drafting/hinge/figures.md, or the attorney waives it in drafting/hinge/findings.md:
- \`figure-coverage\` (figures.md, claim 1): Feature List row F1, which the Draft Outline cites for claim 1, has no drawn part in figures.md. Link a confirmed part under a figure heading to it, e.g. "- 20: <part> [F1]" (37 CFR 1.83(a): the drawings must show every feature specified in the claims).",
  "epoLetter": "The Drawing Set was not built. 1 Error(s) of the figure list are open; fix each in drafting/hinge/figures.md, or the attorney waives it in drafting/hinge/findings.md:
- \`figures-settings\` (figures.md): figures.md sets \`pageSize: letter\`, but the EPO accepts A4 sheets only (OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 2(2)). Set \`pageSize: A4\`.",
  "noFigure": "The Drawing Set was not built. drafting/hinge/drawings/ has no Figure (FIG-N.svg). Render each Figure with render_figure first.",
  "proposed": "The Drawing Set was not built. drafting/hinge/figures.md has 1 proposed part(s); the attorney confirms each by removing "(proposed)", or deletes the line:
- \`figure-proposal\` (figures.md, line 14): Part 8 ("spring") is a proposal from sketches/sketch-1.png: the disclosure does not state it. The attorney confirms it by removing "(proposed)", or deletes the line.",
}
`;

exports[`propose_figure_part > appends a proposed line with the next numeral and copies the attached sketch to sketches/ 1`] = `
{
  "again": "Wrote to drafting/hinge/figures.md: \`- 16: spring (proposed from sketches/bracket-sketch.png)\`. The sketch is at drafting/hinge/sketches/bracket-sketch.png. This part is a proposal: build_drawing_set and the export stay blocked until the attorney confirms it by removing "(proposed)", or deletes the line. Tell the attorney what you proposed and why.",
  "figures": "---
numerals: even
---
## FIG. 1

- 10: housing [F1]
- 12: top face
- 14: bracket [F1] (proposed from sketches/bracket-sketch.png)

## FIG. 2

- 2: measuring a cell temperature [F2]
- 4: comparing the cell temperature
- 6: opening a coolant valve

## FIG. 3

- 16: spring (proposed from sketches/bracket-sketch.png)
",
  "result": "Wrote to drafting/hinge/figures.md: \`- 14: bracket [F1] (proposed from sketches/bracket-sketch.png)\`. The sketch is at drafting/hinge/sketches/bracket-sketch.png. This part is a proposal: build_drawing_set and the export stay blocked until the attorney confirms it by removing "(proposed)", or deletes the line. Tell the attorney what you proposed and why.",
  "sketch": [
    137,
    80,
    78,
    71,
    1,
    2,
    3,
  ],
}
`;

exports[`render_figure > refuses 2D numerals that are not under the Figure heading, listing the lines to add 1`] = `
"The Figure was not rendered. Every numeral in a Figure is a numeral of the figure list (37 CFR 1.84(p)(5); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(2)(i); PCT Rule 11.13(l)). The steps of FIG. 2 take these numerals (\`numerals: even\`), which are not under its heading in drafting/hinge/figures.md:
- 8: close the valve
Add these lines under the FIG. 2 heading, then render again."
`;

exports[`render_figure > refuses a part without a numeral 1`] = `
"The Figure was not rendered. Every part drawn has a numeral, and every numeral is in the figure list:
- Error \`part-without-numeral\` (FIG-1.scene.json): Part "lid" is drawn but has no reference numeral. [CONTEXT.md Figure ("every part drawn has one"); 37 CFR 1.84(p)(5); OJ EPO 2025 A49 Art. 1(2)(i)]
Add the part to the figure list (propose_figure_part when the disclosure does not state it), or remove it from the scene."
`;

exports[`render_figure > renders a 3D scene: writes the source, the SVG and the review render, returns the render with the findings, and records the round 1`] = `
{
  "drawings": [
    "FIG-1.scene.json",
    "FIG-1.svg",
    "review",
    "rounds.json",
  ],
  "first": {
    "images": [
      "image/png",
    ],
    "text": "Rendered FIG. 1: wrote drafting/hinge/drawings/FIG-1.scene.json, drafting/hinge/drawings/FIG-1.svg and the review render drafting/hinge/drawings/review/FIG-1.round-1.png. Round 1 of 3.
The review render of this round is attached; it is not a deliverable.
The mechanical fault list found nothing. The attorney still reviews the Figure.
Do not call the Figure compliant or ready to file.",
  },
  "pngSignature": "PNG",
  "review": [
    "FIG-1.round-1.png",
    "FIG-1.round-2.png",
  ],
  "rounds": {
    "figures": {
      "1": [
        {
          "png": "review/FIG-1.round-1.png",
          "round": 1,
          "seen": true,
        },
        {
          "png": "review/FIG-1.round-2.png",
          "round": 2,
          "seen": false,
        },
      ],
    },
  },
  "second": {
    "images": [],
    "text": "Rendered FIG. 1: wrote drafting/hinge/drawings/FIG-1.scene.json, drafting/hinge/drawings/FIG-1.svg and the review render drafting/hinge/drawings/review/FIG-1.round-2.png. Round 2 of 3.
No render is attached (the model reads the findings only); the receipt records that no render was seen in this round.
The mechanical fault list found nothing. The attorney still reviews the Figure.
Do not call the Figure compliant or ready to file.",
  },
  "sourceFigure": "FIG-1",
  "svgStart": "<svg",
}
`;

exports[`render_figure > renders a flowchart from an approved method claim 1`] = `
{
  "result": {
    "images": [
      "image/png",
    ],
    "text": "Rendered FIG. 2: wrote drafting/hinge/drawings/FIG-2.scene.json, drafting/hinge/drawings/FIG-2.svg and the review render drafting/hinge/drawings/review/FIG-2.round-1.png. Round 1 of 3.
The review render of this round is attached; it is not a deliverable.
The mechanical fault list found nothing. The attorney still reviews the Figure.
Do not call the Figure compliant or ready to file.",
  },
  "source": {
    "figure": "FIG-2",
    "input": {
      "figure": 2,
      "office": "US",
      "scheme": "even",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "s1",
          "text": "measuring a cell temperature with a sensor",
        },
        {
          "id": "s2",
          "text": "comparing the cell temperature with a limit",
        },
        {
          "id": "s3",
          "text": "opening a coolant valve when the cell temperature exceeds the limit",
        },
      ],
    },
    "mode": "flowchart",
  },
}
`;
